		<div class="hidden udot-notice banner notice-info" data-noticeid="72426" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="notice-72426-heading"><div class="banner-header"><h4 id="notice-72426-heading"><a href="https://connect.udot.utah.gov/notices/scam-alert-utah-toll-services/">SCAM ALERT: Multiple fraudulent texts and calls claiming unpaid tolls, tickets, or other infractions &#8211; NOT FROM UDOT OR DMV</a></h4><button class="banner-close" aria-label="Close notice: SCAM ALERT: Multiple fraudulent texts and calls claiming unpaid tolls, tickets, or other infractions &#8211; NOT FROM UDOT OR DMV">Close</button></div><div class="banner-body"><p>We&#8217;ve been made aware that some Utahns are receiving a text message asking for personal information and money for a toll service. <strong>Do not respond or give any information.</strong> This is part of a nation-wide scam. UDOT&#8217;s databases have not been compromised.  Some examples of scam texts are shown below.</p>
<p><strong>Report scams and suspicious communications to the <a href="https://reportfraud.ftc.gov/#/?orgcode=UTDOT" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Federal Trade Commission</a>.</strong></p>
<p>Additional Information:</p>
